How we learn together

We create one 15-second canonical scene, but build it as a reusable system:

1. Define the emotional and narrative beats.
2. Produce a crude animatic immediately.
3. Build one character from separable, reusable parts.
4. Represent the shot in AnimationIR.
5. Generate a Blender scene and animation from it.
6. Render several timing variations.
7. You judge the perceptual deltas.
8. I encode those judgments into our evolving animation grammar.
9. Reuse the character and operators in the next scene.

You learn how to command and evaluate animation. I learn how your language maps to timing, movement, framing and emotion. The artifacts teach both of us.

The right initial spend is therefore $0. Install Blender and DaVinci. Don’t buy anything until the first scene exposes a real bottleneck. Our first investment should be in constructing the shared interface—not accumulating software.